Experiment 6: Memory Allocation & Virtual Memory in C
A comprehensive technical manual investigating virtual memory management, demand paging, physical RAM allocation via 4096-byte MMU page faults, and real-time system monitoring using free -h and watch.
OS LAB WALKTHROUGH — C, LINUX, VIRTUAL MEMORY


Anatomy of a Memory-Allocating C Program
A line-by-line breakdown of a small C program that takes a size in megabytes from the command line, allocates that much memory, actually touches every page of it, holds it open so you can watch it in free -h, and releases it cleanly when Ctrl+C is pressed.
